    "body": "As far as I can tell by looking in the user interface, as stored in the\r\ndb, ip_address, and user_agent are unused and click_time is only used to\r\nthe day, but stored is seconds. Without that data, the data stored in\r\nthe db is pretty safe to call not personally identifiable, which is what\r\nI want, and seems like a good config option that other users would want.\r\n\r\nI know there is an option to not store anything in yourls_log, but the\r\ndata that appears to be actually used, like country, and day of click,\r\nis generally not personally identifiable, so I should be able to keep\r\nthat data.\r\n\r\nAlso, after implementing this, a way to remove old data would be good\r\ntoo.\r\n\r\n### Technical details regarding my environment\r\n\r\n* YOURLS version: 1.7.2\r\n  * Plugins enabled: none\r\n* PHP version: doesn't matter\r\n\r\n### Bug description \r\n\r\n**What is the current behavior?**\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe the current behavior -->\r\n\r\nsee above\r\n\r\n**What is the expected or desired behavior?**\r\n\r\nsee above\r\n\r\n### Reproducible bug summary \r\n\r\nsee above.\r\n\r\n",
